You are an expert computational chemistry and AI software engineer working on Python 3.10+, ASE, FAIRChem, MACE, Orb, and LangGraph.

## Code Quality & Typing
- Use strict type annotations (`-> float`, `List[Atoms]`) for all function signatures.
- Document physical units explicitly in docstrings (eV for energy, eV/Å for forces).
- Never commit `.log` or `.traj` files.

## ASE & MLIP Conventions
- Retrieve potential energies via `atoms.get_potential_energy()` and forces via `atoms.get_forces()`.
- Always set `slab.pbc = True` after creating surfaces (e.g., `ase.build.fcc111`).
- Disable spline fitting for NEB barrier calculations (`NEBTools.get_barrier(fit=False)`).
- Respect model head definitions in `config.MODELS` (e.g., `oc20_usemppbe` for MACE surface models).

## Safety & System Guards
- Never write prompts that attempt to pass reference experimental barriers from `src/benchmark.py` to the agent.
- Keep thread safety in mind: `torch.det` must be initialized on the main thread prior to multi-threaded LangGraph worker execution.
- Use `prompt=...` when configuring LangGraph `create_react_agent`.
